  "verse_case": {
    "VSM_30_11": "írāyai kīnā́śaṃ pairs a dative singular with the accusative singular professional term. The acute of kīnā́śaṃ falls on ā.",
    "TB_3_4_9_1": "The accented Devanāgarī citation and the order of its ten occupational entries are preserved. The two animal-keeper items trade places with their respective datives attached. The last dative has adhyakṣāya, compared with VSM ādhyakṣyāya.",
    "TB_2_4_8_7": "The Maruts are the ploughmen in a nominal plural predication with āsan, while Indra was lord of the plough. This is the second literal occurrence in the entire selected TB file.",
    "cross_source_status": "The two lists exhibit the same occupation in the same case and a third text location gives another use. They do not independently specify an operation of k in kan."
